---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Eurocert Asia"
  description="Read the Eurocert Asia privacy policy covering how personal information is collected, used, protected and managed across website and service interactions."
  canonicalUrl="https://www.eurocert.asia/privacy-policy/"
  ogImage="https://res.cloudinary.com/dwnnakrrh/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1600/v1782367859/eurocert/Untitled_design_19_.png.png"
  keywords="Eurocert,Eurocert Asia,ISO certification,CE marking,food safety certification,FSSC 22000,BRCGS,GFSI,social audits,Sedex,SMETA,SA8000,inspection services,certification body,India,management systems,ISO 9001,ISO 14001,ISO 45001,GDPR,privacy policy,data protection"
>

<style is:global>
  .policy-content h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading), ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #0f172a;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .policy-content h4 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading), ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #1e293b;
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .policy-content p {
    color: #475569;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .policy-content ul {
    list-style: disc;
    color: #475569;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }
  .policy-content ul li {
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
  .policy-content ol {
    list-style: decimal;
    color: #475569;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }
  .policy-content ol li {
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
  .policy-content strong {
    color: #1e293b;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .policy-content a {
    color: #0a2463;
    text-decoration: underline;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }
  .policy-content a:hover {
    color: #1e3a8a;
  }
  .policy-content .section-block {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #f1f5f9;
  }
  .policy-content .section-block:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>

<!-- Hero Section -->
<section class="relative min-h-[50vh] flex items-center justify-center overflow-hidden bg-[#030a16]">
  <div class="absolute inset-0 z-0">
    <img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dwnnakrrh/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1600/v1782367707/eurocert/pp1.png.png" alt="Privacy Policy" class="w-full h-full object-cover" />
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-[#030a16] via-[#030a16]/70 to-[#030a16]/40"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="container mx-auto px-6 relative z-10 text-center py-20">
    <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full border border-eurogold-400/30 bg-eurogold-400/5 mb-6">
      <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-eurogold-400 animate-pulse"></span>
      <span class="heading-font text-[10px] text-eurogold-400 tracking-[0.3em] uppercase font-bold">Data Protection</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="heading-font text-4xl sm:text-6xl md:text-7xl font-bold text-white mb-3 tracking-tight" style="text-shadow:0 0 30px rgba(212,168,67,0.3)">Privacy <span class="text-eurogold-400">Policy</span></h1>
    <p class="text-white/70 text-sm heading-font mt-4">Last Updated: 17 September 2026</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Privacy Policy Content -->
<section class="py-14 lg:py-20 bg-white">
  <div class="container mx-auto px-6">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">

      <!-- Intro -->
      <div class="mb-10">
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-[15px] leading-relaxed">
          Eurocert Inspection Services Pvt. Ltd. ("Eurocert", "we", "us", or "our") respects your privacy and is committed to protecting your personal data.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-[15px] leading-relaxed">
          This Privacy Policy explains how Eurocert collects, uses, stores, protects, and otherwise processes personal data when you visit or use <a href="https://www.eurocert.asia/">https://www.eurocert.asia/</a>, contact us, request our services, participate in certification, inspection, audit or training activities, or otherwise interact with us.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-[15px] leading-relaxed">
          Where applicable, this Privacy Policy is intended to address the requirements of the EU General Data Protection Regulation (Regulation (EU) 2016/679 — GDPR) and other applicable data-protection laws.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-[15px] leading-relaxed">
          By using our website or providing personal data to us, you acknowledge that you have read this Privacy Policy.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="policy-content">

        <!-- Section 1 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>1. Who We Are</h3>
          <p>The data controller responsible for the processing of personal data described in this Privacy Policy is:</p>
          <p><strong>Eurocert Inspection Services Pvt. Ltd.</strong><br />
          Registered/Head Office:<br />
          304, Mid Town Tower, Peer Muchalla,<br />
          Panchkula, Haryana – 134109, India<br />
          Telephone: +91 9316012883<br />
          Email: <a href="mailto:info@eurocert.in">info@eurocert.in</a></p>
          <p>Eurocert Asia is affiliated with Eurocert S.A., Athens, Greece, which forms part of the wider Eurocert network. Depending on the particular service or processing activity, another Eurocert group entity may have a role in processing personal data. Where this occurs, the applicable responsibilities will be determined in accordance with the relevant contractual and legal arrangements.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 2 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>2. Scope of This Privacy Policy</h3>
          <p>This Privacy Policy applies to personal data collected or processed through:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Our website;</li>
            <li>Directly from you when you use our website chatbot or other online chat tools to submit an enquiry, including your name, telephone number, email address and any other information you choose to provide;</li>
            <li>Contact and enquiry forms;</li>
            <li>Certification and inspection enquiries;</li>
            <li>Audit and assessment activities;</li>
            <li>Training registration and related activities;</li>
            <li>Client and prospective-client communications;</li>
            <li>Business communications;</li>
            <li>Complaints, appeals and grievance submissions;</li>
            <li>Recruitment or career enquiries, where applicable;</li>
            <li>Cookies and similar technologies; and</li>
            <li>Other interactions with Eurocert where this Privacy Policy is provided or referenced.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>This Privacy Policy does not necessarily apply to processing performed by third parties independently of Eurocert. Such third parties may have their own privacy policies.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 3 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>3. What Is Personal Data?</h3>
          <p>"Personal data" means information relating to an identified or identifiable individual.</p>
          <p>Depending on how you interact with Eurocert, this may include:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Full name;</li>
            <li>Business or personal email address;</li>
            <li>Telephone or mobile number;</li>
            <li>Company or organisation name;</li>
            <li>Job title or professional information;</li>
            <li>Information contained in enquiries or correspondence;</li>
            <li>Information provided in certification, audit or inspection-related communications;</li>
            <li>Information submitted through grievance or complaint forms;</li>
            <li>Information relating to training or registration;</li>
            <li>Browser and device information;</li>
            <li>Website usage information;</li>
            <li>Cookie identifiers and similar online identifiers;</li>
            <li>Information contained in documents provided to us; and</li>
            <li>Other information that you voluntarily provide to us.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>We aim to collect only personal data that is relevant and reasonably necessary for the relevant purpose.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 4 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>4. How We Collect Personal Data</h3>
          <p>We may collect personal data:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Directly from you when you complete a form or contact us;</li>
            <li>When you request certification, inspection, audit, training or other services;</li>
            <li>When you communicate with our employees, auditors, assessors or representatives;</li>
            <li>When you submit documents or information required for a service;</li>
            <li>Automatically when you use our website, including through cookies and similar technologies;</li>
            <li>From your organisation or employer where you are participating in a business or certification relationship; and</li>
            <li>From third parties where permitted by applicable law and necessary for providing our services.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 5 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>5. Purposes for Which We Process Personal Data</h3>
          <p>We may process personal data for the following purposes:</p>

          <h4>5.1 Providing Our Services</h4>
          <p>To:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Respond to enquiries;</li>
            <li>Provide certification, inspection, audit and assessment services;</li>
            <li>Manage client relationships;</li>
            <li>Process applications and requests;</li>
            <li>Arrange audits, inspections, assessments and training;</li>
            <li>Communicate with clients and prospective clients;</li>
            <li>Issue and manage certificates and related records;</li>
            <li>Maintain service and certification records; and</li>
            <li>Provide technical or administrative support.</li>
          </ul>

          <h4>5.2 Business Communications</h4>
          <p>We may use contact information to communicate with you regarding:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Your enquiry;</li>
            <li>Requested services;</li>
            <li>Existing business relationships;</li>
            <li>Service updates;</li>
            <li>Certification or audit activities;</li>
            <li>Administrative matters; and</li>
            <li>Other communications relevant to our relationship.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Where marketing communications require consent under applicable law, we will obtain the necessary consent.</p>

          <h4>5.3 Legal and Regulatory Compliance</h4>
          <p>We may process personal data where necessary to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Comply with applicable laws and regulations;</li>
            <li>Meet accreditation requirements;</li>
            <li>Respond to lawful requests from competent authorities;</li>
            <li>Maintain required records;</li>
            <li>Establish, exercise or defend legal claims; and</li>
            <li>Detect, prevent or investigate fraud, misuse or security incidents.</li>
          </ul>

          <h4>5.4 Website Operation and Security</h4>
          <p>We may process technical information to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Operate and maintain the website;</li>
            <li>Protect website security;</li>
            <li>Detect malicious or unauthorised activity;</li>
            <li>Troubleshoot technical problems;</li>
            <li>Monitor website performance; and</li>
            <li>Improve website functionality.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 6 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>6. Legal Bases for Processing Under the GDPR</h3>
          <p>Where the GDPR applies, we process personal data only where an appropriate legal basis exists.</p>
          <p>Depending on the circumstances, the legal basis may include:</p>

          <h4>6.1 Consent</h4>
          <p>We may process personal data where you have provided valid consent.</p>
          <p>You may withdraw consent at any time. Withdrawal of consent does not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out before withdrawal.</p>

          <h4>6.2 Contract</h4>
          <p>Processing may be necessary to enter into or perform a contract with you or your organisation.</p>
          <p>For example, this may apply when processing information necessary to provide certification, inspection, audit or training services.</p>

          <h4>6.3 Legal Obligation</h4>
          <p>We may process personal data where processing is necessary to comply with a legal or regulatory obligation applicable to Eurocert.</p>

          <h4>6.4 Legitimate Interests</h4>
          <p>We may process personal data where necessary for our legitimate interests, provided that those interests are not overridden by your fundamental rights and freedoms.</p>
          <p>Examples may include:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Managing business relationships;</li>
            <li>Maintaining information security;</li>
            <li>Preventing fraud or misuse;</li>
            <li>Protecting our systems and services;</li>
            <li>Improving our services; and</li>
            <li>Establishing or defending legal claims.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Where we rely on legitimate interests, we will consider the impact of the processing on individuals and apply appropriate safeguards.</p>

          <h4>6.5 Vital Interests</h4>
          <p>Where applicable, personal data may be processed where necessary to protect someone's vital interests.</p>

          <h4>6.6 Public Task</h4>
          <p>Where applicable, processing may be carried out where necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 7 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>7. Data Minimisation</h3>
          <p>We follow the principle of data minimisation.</p>
          <p>This means that we seek to collect and process personal data that is:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Adequate;</li>
            <li>Relevant; and</li>
            <li>Limited to what is necessary for the purposes for which it is processed.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>We do not intentionally collect unnecessary personal information through our website.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 8 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>8. Accuracy of Personal Data</h3>
          <p>We take reasonable steps to ensure that personal data we process is accurate and, where necessary, kept up to date.</p>
          <p>You may contact us if you believe that information we hold about you is inaccurate or incomplete.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 9 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>9. Data Retention</h3>
          <p>We retain personal data only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes for which it was collected, including where necessary to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Provide requested services;</li>
            <li>Maintain certification, audit or inspection records;</li>
            <li>Comply with legal, regulatory or accreditation requirements;</li>
            <li>Resolve disputes;</li>
            <li>Establish or defend legal claims;</li>
            <li>Maintain business records; or</li>
            <li>Enforce our agreements.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Different categories of information may be retained for different periods.</p>
          <p>When personal data is no longer required, we will delete, securely destroy, or anonymise it, subject to applicable legal, regulatory and accreditation requirements.</p>
          <p>Specific retention periods should be documented in Eurocert's internal data-retention schedule.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 10 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>10. Sharing of Personal Data</h3>
          <p>We do not sell or rent personal data.</p>
          <p>We may disclose personal data where necessary and lawful to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Eurocert group companies or affiliated entities;</li>
            <li>Auditors, inspectors, assessors and technical experts;</li>
            <li>Accreditation bodies;</li>
            <li>Certification scheme owners;</li>
            <li>Regulatory authorities and government bodies;</li>
            <li>Professional advisers;</li>
            <li>IT, hosting, security and technical service providers;</li>
            <li>Communication and email service providers;</li>
            <li>Other service providers acting on our behalf; and</li>
            <li>Courts, law-enforcement authorities or other competent authorities where legally required.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Where third parties process personal data on our behalf, we seek to ensure that appropriate contractual and organisational safeguards are in place as required by applicable law.</p>
          <p>We will not disclose personal data to third parties for unrelated purposes unless permitted or required by law.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 11 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>11. International Transfers</h3>
          <p>Eurocert operates in an international business environment and may work with clients, auditors, certification bodies, accreditation organisations and service providers located in different countries.</p>
          <p>Where personal data subject to the GDPR is transferred outside the European Economic Area ("EEA"), we will take appropriate steps to ensure that the transfer is carried out in accordance with applicable data-protection law.</p>
          <p>Depending on the circumstances, this may include:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>An adequacy decision adopted by the European Commission;</li>
            <li>Standard Contractual Clauses approved by the European Commission;</li>
            <li>Binding Corporate Rules, where applicable;</li>
            <li>Another lawful transfer mechanism recognised under applicable law; or</li>
            <li>A permitted derogation for specific circumstances.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Information concerning the specific transfer mechanism may be provided upon request where required by applicable law.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 12 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>12. Data Security</h3>
          <p>Eurocert takes reasonable and appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect personal data against:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Unauthorised access;</li>
            <li>Unauthorised disclosure;</li>
            <li>Accidental loss;</li>
            <li>Destruction;</li>
            <li>Alteration;</li>
            <li>Unauthorised processing; and</li>
            <li>Other unlawful or accidental forms of processing.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Depending on the nature and risk of the processing, security measures may include:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Access controls;</li>
            <li>Authentication controls;</li>
            <li>Role-based access;</li>
            <li>Security monitoring;</li>
            <li>Data backup;</li>
            <li>Network and system security;</li>
            <li>Encryption or pseudonymisation where appropriate;</li>
            <li>Secure transmission mechanisms;</li>
            <li>Staff confidentiality obligations;</li>
            <li>Security policies and procedures;</li>
            <li>Vulnerability and security management; and</li>
            <li>Incident response procedures.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>No method of transmission or storage can be guaranteed to be completely secure. However, we continuously seek to maintain appropriate safeguards based on the risks associated with our processing activities.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 13 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>13. Privacy by Design and by Default</h3>
          <p>Where appropriate, Eurocert seeks to consider data-protection and privacy requirements when designing or implementing systems, processes and services.</p>
          <p>This may include:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Data minimisation;</li>
            <li>Access restrictions;</li>
            <li>Appropriate security controls;</li>
            <li>Limited retention;</li>
            <li>Privacy-conscious configuration; and</li>
            <li>Appropriate technical and organisational safeguards.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 14 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>14. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h3>
          <p>Our website may use cookies and similar technologies.</p>
          <p>Cookies may be used for purposes such as:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Website functionality;</li>
            <li>Security;</li>
            <li>Remembering preferences;</li>
            <li>Analytics;</li>
            <li>Performance monitoring; and</li>
            <li>Other website-related purposes.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Where required by applicable law, non-essential cookies and similar technologies will be used only after obtaining the appropriate consent.</p>
          <p>You may manage cookie preferences through the cookie-consent mechanism provided on the website and, where applicable, through your browser settings.</p>
          <p>Please note that disabling certain cookies may affect website functionality.</p>
          <p>Eurocert should maintain a separate Cookie Policy/Cookie Notice identifying the actual cookies, providers, purposes, duration and legal basis used on the website.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 15 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>15. Your Data Protection Rights</h3>
          <p>Where the GDPR applies, you may have the following rights, subject to applicable legal conditions and exceptions:</p>

          <h4>Right of Access</h4>
          <p>You may request confirmation as to whether we process your personal data and, where applicable, request access to that data.</p>

          <h4>Right to Rectification</h4>
          <p>You may request correction of inaccurate or incomplete personal data.</p>

          <h4>Right to Erasure</h4>
          <p>You may request deletion of personal data in circumstances where the GDPR provides a right to erasure.</p>
          <p>This right is not absolute. We may be required to retain certain information to comply with legal, regulatory, contractual or accreditation obligations.</p>

          <h4>Right to Restriction of Processing</h4>
          <p>You may request restriction of processing in circumstances provided by applicable law.</p>

          <h4>Right to Data Portability</h4>
          <p>Where applicable, you may request certain personal data in a structured, commonly used and machine-readable format and request its transmission to another controller where the legal requirements are satisfied.</p>

          <h4>Right to Object</h4>
          <p>You may object to certain processing based on your particular circumstances, including processing based on legitimate interests.</p>
          <p>You have an absolute right to object to processing of your personal data for direct marketing purposes.</p>

          <h4>Right to Withdraw Consent</h4>
          <p>Where processing is based on consent, you may withdraw your consent at any time.</p>
          <p>Withdrawal does not affect processing carried out lawfully before the withdrawal.</p>

          <h4>Rights Relating to Automated Decision-Making</h4>
          <p>Where applicable, you may have rights concerning decisions based solely on automated processing, including profiling, where such decisions produce legal or similarly significant effects.</p>
          <p>Eurocert will provide applicable safeguards where such processing falls within the relevant GDPR provisions.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 16 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>16. How to Exercise Your Rights</h3>
          <p>To exercise your privacy rights, contact:</p>
          <p><strong>Data Protection / Privacy Contact</strong><br />
          Eurocert Inspection Services Pvt. Ltd.<br />
          304, Mid Town Tower, Peer Muchalla,<br />
          Panchkula, Haryana – 134109, India<br />
          Email: <a href="mailto:info@eurocert.in">info@eurocert.in</a></p>
          <p>Please provide sufficient information to allow us to identify you and understand your request.</p>
          <p>We may need to request additional information to verify your identity before processing certain requests.</p>
          <p>We will respond to valid requests within the timeframe required by applicable data-protection law.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 17 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>17. Complaints</h3>
          <p>If you have concerns regarding how Eurocert processes your personal data, we encourage you to contact us first so that we can investigate and address your concern.</p>
          <p>You may also have the right to lodge a complaint with the competent data-protection supervisory authority in accordance with applicable law.</p>
          <p>Where the GDPR applies, you may generally lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority, particularly in the EU Member State of your habitual residence, place of work, or where you believe an infringement occurred.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 18 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>18. Personal Data Breaches</h3>
          <p>Eurocert maintains procedures for identifying, assessing, responding to and documenting personal-data incidents.</p>
          <p>Where a personal-data breach occurs, we will assess the incident and take appropriate corrective and mitigation measures.</p>
          <p>Where required by the GDPR, Eurocert will notify the competent supervisory authority without undue delay and, where feasible, within 72 hours after becoming aware of the breach, unless the breach is unlikely to result in a risk to the rights and freedoms of individuals.</p>
          <p>Where a breach is likely to result in a high risk to individuals' rights and freedoms, we will communicate the breach to affected individuals where required by applicable law.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 19 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>19. Special Categories of Personal Data</h3>
          <p>Certain categories of personal data receive additional protection under the GDPR, including health data, genetic data, biometric data used for identification, racial or ethnic origin, political opinions, religious or philosophical beliefs, trade-union membership, and information concerning sex life or sexual orientation.</p>
          <p>Eurocert does not intentionally request special-category personal data through its general website contact forms unless it is necessary for a specific legitimate business, certification, audit, inspection, legal or regulatory purpose.</p>
          <p>Where special-category personal data is processed, we will apply the additional legal requirements and safeguards applicable to such processing.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 20 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>20. Children's Privacy</h3>
          <p>Our website and professional services are primarily intended for businesses, professionals and organisations.</p>
          <p>We do not knowingly collect personal data from children for purposes that are inappropriate or unlawful.</p>
          <p>If you believe that a child has provided personal data to us without appropriate authorisation, please contact us so that we can investigate and take appropriate action.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 21 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>21. Third-Party Websites</h3>
          <p>Our website may contain links to external websites, platforms or services.</p>
          <p>Eurocert is not responsible for the privacy practices, security, content or policies of third-party websites.</p>
          <p>We recommend reviewing the privacy policy of any external website before providing personal information.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 22 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>22. Third-Party Service Providers</h3>
          <p>We may use third-party service providers to support the operation of our website and business activities.</p>
          <p>Depending on the services used, these providers may provide:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Website hosting;</li>
            <li>Cloud infrastructure;</li>
            <li>Email services;</li>
            <li>Security services;</li>
            <li>Analytics;</li>
            <li>Communication services;</li>
            <li>Website maintenance;</li>
            <li>Document management; or</li>
            <li>Other technical or professional services.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Where a third party processes personal data on our behalf, we will take appropriate steps to ensure that the processing is governed by appropriate contractual and security safeguards where required by applicable law.</p>
          <p>The website owner should maintain an internal register of processors and service providers and update this section where public disclosure is appropriate.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 23 -->
        <div class="section-block">
          <h3>23. Data Protection Officer / Privacy Contact</h3>
          <p>Where Eurocert is legally required to appoint a Data Protection Officer ("DPO"), the DPO or designated privacy contact can be contacted at:</p>
          <p>Email: <a href="mailto:info@eurocert.in">info@eurocert.in</a></p>
          <p>Any DPO designation, representative details, or additional contact details required by applicable law should be added here once formally confirmed.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 24 -->
